      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What equipment can STS recycle?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS accepts computers, laptops, servers, networking equipment, monitors, printers, copy machines, phones, cables, batteries, and other business electronics. Pickup planning can include mixed equipment streams, data-bearing devices, and larger technology refresh projects."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards does STS reference?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS projects may reference NIST 800-88 media sanitization guidance, HIPAA safeguards, ISO 27001 controls, SOC 2 considerations, and DoD 5220.22-M procedures where applicable. The project scope determines which records and handling steps are appropriate."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup timing depends on equipment volume, loading access, service area, and scheduling needs. Many organizations receive a prompt assessment and can arrange same-week pickup. Contact STS with an approximate inventory for a practical scheduling estimate."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Depending on the project, documentation can include pickup records, asset details, certificates of destruction, material disposition information, and downstream reporting. These records help procurement, IT, facilities, and environmental teams maintain a consistent retirement file."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup free for Bakersfield businesses?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Complimentary pickup is available for qualifying volumes and project conditions. STS reviews the equipment type, quantity, access requirements, and service area before confirming logistics. Smaller projects can still request an assessment and available options."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens after equipment is collected?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment is staged, identified, and routed according to the project scope. Data-bearing media can receive destruction or sanitization services, while recoverable components and commodities move through documented downstream channels for material recovery."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How does commercial electronic recycling work in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Commercial electronic recycling combines pickup planning, data handling, asset records, and downstream reporting. Bakersfield organizations can coordinate equipment removal, identify data-bearing devices, document serial numbers when requested, and route materials through appropriate channels for recovery."
          }
        },
